.TH DWGPROBE "1" "July 2026" "dwgprobe 0.14" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dwgprobe \- probe DWG object-map statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwgprobe
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,DWGFILE|DIR\/\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Probes DWG files and prints a Markdown table with object counts, object
record sizes, address ranges, the decode mode used by the probe, whether the
input came from a file map or heap buffer, and sampled RSS when the platform
exposes it. The table also includes the ratio between declared
object record bytes and file bytes, plus a conservative precheck label for
large object records, high object-byte expansion, or very high object counts.
The command reports unsupported stream versions directly, without expanding
them through the full decoder.
Unsupported DWG versions are reported in the table but do not make the command
fail; missing files and critical read errors still do.
.PP
When a directory is passed, dwgprobe scans the directory itself for files
ending in .dwg. It does not recurse into child directories.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display this help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.PP
